 10 are entirely 0, and both become 2.\n- **Pair 2:** row 8 and column 8 are entirely 0, and both become 2, crossing at (8,8).\n- **Pair 3:** rows 2 and 12 and column 1 are entirely 0, and all three become 2.\n\nThe other 0 cells stay 0, even when they touch a line, such as the 0 at (6,0) in pair 3. So the rule is: **every row or column consisting entirely of 0 is recoloured to 2**. Nothing else changes.\n\nThese colours are the same in every pair, so they can be constants:\n- the line colour is always 0,\n- the new colour is always 2.\n\nThe background varies from pair to pair, but the rule never needs it.\n\n## Applying it to the test\n\nThe test grid is 27×25, with background 4.\n- Rows 2, 12 and 20 are all 0.\n- Columns 6 and 21 are all 0.\n\nThe program detects these lines by checking the whole row or column, not by position. It paints the full rows first and then the full columns, so the output is the test grid with a lattice of 2-lines.\n\n## Teaching stages\n\n1. Emit the canvas after recolouring all full 0 rows.\n2. Emit the canvas after also recolouring all full 0 columns (the final answer).\n\nIf a grid has no full rows, step 1 is skipped. In pair 1, for example, only columns change.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    full_rows = [y for y in range(H) if np.all(grid[y, :] == 0)]\n    full_cols = [x for x in range(W) if np.all(grid[:, x] == 0)]\n    if full_rows:\n        for y in full_rows:\n            g[y, :] = 2\n        emit(g, f\"Rows {full_rows} are entirely 0 from edge to edge, so they are divider lines: recolour them to 2.\")\n    for x in full_cols:\n        g[:, x] = 2\n    emit(g, f\"Columns {full_cols} are entirely 0 top to bottom: recolour them to 2 as well. All other 0 cells stay as they are.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Rows [8] are entirely 0 from edge to edge, so they are divider lines: recolour them to 2."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Rows [2, 12] are entirely 0 from edge to edge, so they are divider lines: recolour them to 2."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Rows [2, 12, 20] are entirely 0 from edge to edge, so they are divider lines: recolour them to 2."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So the rule is: **every row or column consisting entirely of 0 is recoloured to 2**."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Emit the canvas after recolouring all full 0 rows."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Emit the canvas after also recolouring all full 0 columns (the final answer)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"c3000c09a569050eccae4a9651293dfc6fe684b7dd656663437e1fd17faafe5c","task_sha256":"e1bda418b5e88b87b467f55fa1f13df4487a51001ef49dac5d154459d01fc5ec","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
